conda-forge/smesh-feedstock recipe/patches/0004-occt-8.0-compat.patch, the NETGENPlugin
part: the OCCT 8.0 pass on NETGENPlugin (NETGENPlugin V9_16_0).

Source: conda-forge/smesh-feedstock, `recipe/patches/0004-occt-8.0-compat.patch`, commit
c54d26ae6 ("Fix build against OCCT 8.0.0", 2026-06-23), its sections on
`src/SMESH/src/NETGENPlugin/src/NETGENPlugin/`. pySMESH dropped them from
`patches/occt8/0004-occt-8.0-compat.patch` while NETGEN was not built (git 682b7ff4f).

Re-ported to NETGENPlugin V9_16_0 by pySMESH. Every hunk applies at fuzz 0. The OCCT 8.0
changes:

* Bnd_B3d.hxx is gone; Bnd_B3.hxx declares `using Bnd_B3d = Bnd_B3<double>`
  (NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx, NETGENPlugin_Remesher_2D.cxx).
* The TopTools_*Iterator* instantiation headers are gone; the collection headers declare
  the iterators (NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx, NETGENPlugin_NETGEN_3D.cxx, which also includes
  TopTools_MapOfShape.hxx that OCCT 8 headers no longer pull in).
* Standard_Failure::DynamicType()->Name() becomes Standard_Failure::ExceptionType()
  (NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx, NETGENPlugin_NETGEN_2D_ONLY.cxx, NETGENPlugin_NETGEN_3D.cxx
  twice).

Changes from the conda-forge text: the sections are re-based on V9_16_0 (the line numbers
moved); the conda hunk that adds TopTools_MapOfShape.hxx to NETGENPlugin_NETGEN_2D_ONLY.cxx
is not needed there and is left out; the looooo/SMESH NETGENPlugin_occt781.patch (the
Link hasher of NCollection_Map) is upstream in V9_16_0 (NETGENPlugin_Mesher.cxx:159-180).

